AB  - Dissolved organic P (DOP) release was measured on natural [plankton] populations of a brackish lagoon in Ivory Coast (West Africa). DOP mean excretion is 8% of net P absorption, and represents 1.7% h-1 of the biomass. Only 28% of biomass is involved in rapid uptake and excretion. Release of P is inversely proportional to the particulate C:particulatre N ratio of the seston and the dissolved P concentration.
